# 🔥 QA Protocol — Feature Not Done Until Tested

> **Assume users break things. Prove it works. Break it yourself first.**

---

## 🔐 Test Credentials

```
Email: test.employe.1@gmail.com
Pass:  admin@123
```

---

## ✅ Mandatory Test Flow

### 1. Auth
- Login succeeds with valid creds
- Login fails gracefully with invalid creds

### 2. Happy Path
```
Create → Read → Update → Delete → Refresh (still persisted?)
```

### 3. Break It
| Attack | Expected |
|--------|----------|
| Empty input | Validation error |
| Wrong format | Helpful error |
| Expired token | Redirect to login |
| Unauthorized | 403 + message |
| Huge payload | Rejection |

### 4. Edge Cases
- Empty states
- Min/max values
- Special chars & emojis
- Rapid double-click
- Refresh mid-mutation
- Slow network

### 5. Security
- User sees ONLY their data
- Cross-org access blocked
- Role permissions enforced

### 6. UI States
```
✅ Loading indicator
✅ Error message
✅ Empty state
✅ Success feedback
✅ Disabled during submit
```

---

## 🧪 Quick Test Matrix

```
Feature: [Name]

Functional
[ ] Create  [ ] Read  [ ] Update  [ ] Delete  [ ] Search  [ ] Pagination

Failures
[ ] Validation  [ ] API errors  [ ] 401/403  [ ] Network timeout

States
[ ] Loading  [ ] Empty  [ ] Error  [ ] Success

Security
[ ] Org isolation  [ ] Role check  [ ] No data leak
```

---

## 🚨 Not Complete If

- Only happy path tested
- No error scenarios verified
- Edge cases skipped
- Auth/permissions unchecked
- UI states missing

---

## 🧼 Before Closing

```
❌ console.log
❌ Debug code
❌ Hardcoded test data
❌ Dev shortcuts
```

---

## 🌐 API Test Template

```bash
# Login
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"test.employe.1@gmail.com","password":"admin@123"}' \
  | jq -r '.accessToken')

# Test endpoint
curl -s http://localhost:8085/api/v1/[endpoint] \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq
```
